From 6db912bb4b4b3b8d9706a7750602c7202128d796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:17:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a hub card completed on a pool worker is
 verified on the hub; chat-tasks keeps released closed cards

A completion binds its receipts (pr_acceptance, goal_verified) by task_events.id, which is local to one
board file. A hub-homed card run on a pool worker completes on the worker's board; the Board feed replays
its events onto the hub with new ids and remaps run_id, but not the JSON payload. On the hub the payload id
named another card's event or none, so completion_verdict never verified it, the origin ledger never
released it, and the MacBook chat listed done hub cards t_01a1d41478234144, t_01a1d44d87ea4bef and
t_01a1d4eead55e393 as `unknown` for hours (2026-11-13). On the live hub all four cards' payload ids
(1392472, 486557, 179773, 181582) resolve to nothing, while each card's receipt sits one id before its
completion in the same run (1185670 before 1185671, ...).

- complete_task now also records each receipt's stable uid (`*_event_uid`), which the feed carries
  unchanged. kanban_completion_refs binds by uid when present (no integer fallback). For a pre-uid
  completion replayed from another gateway whose integer does not name this card's receipt here, it binds
  the latest receipt of that kind the same gateway wrote in the same run before the completion. On its own
  board that is the one complete_task bound, because it writes receipt and completion in one transaction.
  A completion that names no receipt never borrows one, and a local completion with a wrong id stays
  unverified. Both readers use it: observe_owner_task (row-by-row) and read_completions (batch).
- replica_cards: a reader that asks for closed cards (`hermes kanban chat-tasks` passes done/archived) now
  keeps a chat's released link to a closed remote card. It shows as an explicit row with status done or
  archived, released=True, unfinished=False and release_reason=link_released, instead of vanishing.
  Worker-homed done cards (t_01a1d4e38cf61e24, PR #2227) were released by _owner_written_releases and
  dropped from chat-tasks within minutes; t_01a1d4f2f591d595 was linked with `chat-tasks --expect` rc=0 and
  then disappeared. The sidebar counts and handover read open statuses only, so they are unchanged.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_completion_refs_sync.py (a worker completion replayed through the Board
feed onto a hub with a longer history, verified by both readers; pre-uid fallback; guards) and
test_kanban_chat_links.py::test_a_released_link_to_a_closed_card_stays_listed_as_done_for_a_reader_of_closed_cards.
On origin/main e3334630da three of these fail, the guards pass; with the change, 159 tests across chat_links,
chat_links_parity, completion_refs_sync, pr_acceptance, goal_receipt, execution_receipt and origin_ledger pass.

Kanban: t_01a1d5319dcf3c16
